	(descr "BAT Wireless BWSMA-KE-Z001, SMA jack (K=hole/female), straight vertical PCB-end THT connector, board-edge mount, 0-6 GHz, 50 Ohm (LCSC C496549, https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C496549.html). Land pattern per BAT Wireless mechanical drawing PCB Layout: 4x GND legs on a 5.08x5.08mm square (Ø1.4mm drill each), center Signal pin on-axis (Ø1.4mm drill), all 5 holes called out '5-Ø1.4' on the datasheet. Ground/signal pad copper sizes and roundrect ratio follow the stock KiCad SMA_BAT_Wireless_BWSMA-KWE-Z001 footprint's pad geometry, which was cross-checked against this drawing and found to use effectively the same pitch (2.55mm vs datasheet's exact 2.54mm) and identical 1.4mm drill - see task report for details; the KWE footprint's elongated Fab/Courtyard outline (representing a right-angle body overhang) was NOT reused since BWSMA-KE-Z001 is a straight/vertical jack with a compact ~6.5x6.5mm square flange per its own drawing.")
